# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets headers (CLA-266). Mirrors the retired vercel.json header table:
# every asset keeps WebMCP to this origin; the top-level shells are origin-keyed (Origin-Agent-Cluster).
# These rules apply only to what the Worker passes through env.ASSETS. Worker-owned routes (/r/*, /og/*,
# /oembed, /scan/*, /api/*) and the Worker-rendered home (GET/HEAD `/` and `/index.html` with no query or only
# search/sort/tracking params, CLA-269) set their own headers in apps/edge, WebMCP ones included. The blocks
# for `/` and `/index.html` still cover the SPA shell those paths serve for any other query (`/?fixture=okie`).
# /new never reaches Static Assets any more (GET/HEAD 301 to `/`; other methods are answered by the Worker),
# so it has no block.
/*
  Permissions-Policy: tools=(self)

/
  Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?1

/index.html
  Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?1

# Vite content-hashes everything under /assets/, so it never changes in place.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
